Here is a Java solution to determine if an integer n is a power of three: 

```
public boolean isPowerOfThree(int n) {
    if (n <= 0) {
        return false;
    }
    while (n % 3 == 0) {
        n /= 3;
    }
    return n == 1;
}
```

This solution uses a loop to divide the input integer by 3 until it is no longer divisible. If the result is 1, then the input is a power of three and the method returns true. Otherwise, the input is not a power of three and the method returns false. If the input integer is negative, or zero, the method returns false.

